                        "entry_id": "63bfe278-9441-370e-bc84-8343d48b3f46",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who feels secure, but who may in fact not be."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ced06111-12d8-4b46-8137-1844c932c2a8",
                                "sense_id": "73a64125-afe4-37c8-8b5f-86032cbaca53",
                                "text": "The sensual Securitan pleases himself in the conceit of his own peace."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5bcea3c7-d0e6-4b6c-b830-0babb2b11184",
                                "sense_id": "73a64125-afe4-37c8-8b5f-86032cbaca53",
                                "text": "The dissolute securitans think that God doth but smile at the absurdities of men ; that ludit in humanis ; that their drunkenness and adulteries rather make him merry than angry."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f3dd78d-dac3-441e-a34c-682f80bcefd2",
                                "sense_id": "73a64125-afe4-37c8-8b5f-86032cbaca53",
                                "text": "As we said, it is fighting without aggression and is declared against the fighters, not against securitans and peaceful people, who are not dangerous to the Islamic Call or the Islamic community."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
